message: "If you use this software, results or protocol, please cite it as below, and cite the article once it is published."
title: "CINETRA: A Multi-Vendor Audit of Semantic Concept Transfer in Cardiac MRI (code, protocol and frozen results)"
type: software
version: v1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23269591
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23269591
    description: "Zenodo archive, all versions (resolves to the latest)"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23269592
    description: "Zenodo archive of v1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/radiukpavlo/transition-matrix-cinetra"
license: [MIT, CC-BY-4.0, CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0]
abstract: >-
  CINETRA audits a frozen multinomial logistic regression on 57 mask descriptors of cine cardiac MRI: a typed
  transition maps the descriptors to measured ventricular concepts, variable-precision rough-set rules must pass a
  cross-fitted gate, and every case receives a reason-coded label or computational abstention. This repository holds
  the registered protocol CMR-TRANS-AUDIT 6.0.1, the code that produced the results (byte-identical to the
  registered commit), the aggregate results of the frozen run, the bundles fitted on the ACDC development set, and
  the tools to verify the registration and reproduce the study.
keywords:
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - cardiac magnetic resonance imaging
  - transition matrix
  - rough sets
  - concept-based explanation
  - distribution shift
  - selective prediction
  - registered protocol
